045417] [17592186145200 #edb/ref 1080 "48cm^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145200 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145200 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5705ed1e-732e-5533-a139-19d387ba009f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145201 #edb/ref 1080 "66cm^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145201 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145201 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d19c501-bc52-501a-b51e-47c81cf51809" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147296 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147296 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the surface area of the triangular prism represented by the net below?\n\n![](images/da/dafb07440f60418465b579aad73119cd47d6def34ed0cf1229afc9affbb177e4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0803c5b9-51e2-5d4e-9c8f-cd8d575a7bec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147296 #edb/ref 1074 "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (side faces).\n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSurface area &= 2 \\cdot (Area of base) + 3 \\cdot (Area of side) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 12 + 3 \\cdot 48 \\\\\n&= 24 + 144 \\\\\n&= 168cm^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147298 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2762" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147298 #edb/ref 1071 "Maggy is building a pyramid from a cardboard net, shown below. What will be the total surface area of the pyramid?\n\n![](images/29/29c918514e60da13363883770befd9d80098deaba0b45cfcafa3255feb143261.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147298 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c91d73c6-cb1f-55d2-986b-83f94a6a66ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147298 #edb/ref 1074 "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangular base and $3$ triangular sides.\n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSurface area &= 1 \\cdot (Area of base) + 3 \\cdot (Area of side) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 10 + 3 \\cdot 12 \\\\\n&= 10 + 36 \\\\\n&= 46in^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147304 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147304 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fe/fe43d65b35d583b21f25977a738e758a31d6b04eb08957877879cc54eef3f45f.png)\n\nBy assuming that all of the side faces have the same height $(8\\,\\text{in})$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above by considering its net." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "80466688-43e1-5697-976c-6ba63844fed9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147304 #edb/ref 1074 "The net of our pyramid is as follows:\n\n![](images/c4/c4a5fe995aaaf47b7ab2b90492059d739fc2352955dc1e12a71852fc13046a33.png)\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with sides equal to $5 \\, \\text{in}$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of square} = 5 \\times 5 = 25 \\, \\text{in}^2\n$$\n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $5\\,\\text{in}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{in}$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 8 = 20 \\, \\text{in}^2\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (the base) and $4$ triangles (the side faces).\n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSurface area &= 1 \\cdot (Area of the square) + 4 \\cdot (Area of the triangle) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 25 + 4 \\cdot 20 \\\\\n&= 25 + 80 \\\\\n&= 105in^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147617 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147618 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186148152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147622 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding Surface Areas Using Nets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186148632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147669 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "d4581297-2bc3-59f4-ac33-21c38ab0b891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147907 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147907 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147907 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0c/0cb01fa25e07a0f18655c9b61b732ca0738ea6fbe735422f92925a7dcc6963be.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism represented by the net above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147907 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c68b4c0-9bb1-5498-b122-47cadbc90d21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148598 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148598 #edb/ref 1061 9274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148598 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "094123eb-863d-53d0-bffd-d4af3cbc5c8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148598 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148599 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148599 #edb/ref 1061 9275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148599 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c579d029-acc2-5cf5-b5cb-0d74e29dc095" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148599 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148603 #edb/ref 1061 9294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148603 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f37e8c00-7648-50da-a5ea-514aa04c1594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148603 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148632 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148632 #edb/ref 1061 9709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148632 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb350109-9beb-546a-a0c5-41e6f139bab5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148632 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148633 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148633 #edb/ref 1061 9710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cf84acc6-2c16-5427-b489-739a60c4925d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148726 #edb/ref 1064 "The **surface area** of a polyhedron is the combined area of all its faces.\n\nTo calculate the surface area of a polyhedron, we use nets.\n\nLet's consider the net of the rectangular pyramid below. What is the surface area of this pyramid?\n\n![](images/7f/7f1843bc6f3c0e331b99045c731368771f831abdccdb7c255606d39a0fb616e4.png)\n\nThe surface area of our pyramid consists of one rectangle (the base) and four triangles (the side faces).\n\nAlso, notice that there are two different triangular faces:\n\n- there are two triangular faces with an area of $60\\,\\text{in}^2$, and\n- there are two triangular faces with an area of $30\\,\\text{in}^2$.\n\nCalculating the total area, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSurface area &= 1 \\cdot 120in^{2} + 2 \\cdot 60in^{2} + 2 \\cdot 30in^{2} \\\\\n&= 120in^{2} + 120in^{2} + 60in^{2} \\\\\n&= 300in^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the surface area of the pyramid is $300 \\, \\text{in}^2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148726 #edb/ref 1065 2329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148726 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e2c9b151-2ae3-545d-aecf-0d7faa137775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148726 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148727 #edb/ref 1064 "If we know a polyhedron's measurements, we can calculate its surface area by first drawing the net of the polyhedron. Then, we calculate the areas of its polygonal faces using known formulas and then sum the results.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find the surface area of the rectangular prism shown below.\n\n![](images/85/85ddfbae506653a6b2c4982be74f9eff2b91df55a5075597ddbbd42a51cc2f52.png)\n\nFirst, we consider the net of our prism.\n\n![](images/98/9874d746b2510403accdbd2e9d77ce8d5bc917b76e68c3f1690a24e8643ad473.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the prism is made up of squares and rectangles.\n\n- The rectangles are $8\\,\\text{ft}$ long and $2\\,\\text{ft}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is\n$\\text{Area of rectangle} = 8 \\times 2 = 16 \\, \\text{ft}^2$.\n- The squares have sides of length $2\\, \\text{ft}$. So, the area of one square is\n$\\text{Area of square} = 2 \\times 2 = 4 \\, \\text{ft}^2$.\n\nFinally, the surface area of the prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares.\n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSurface area &= 4 \\cdot (Area of rectangle) + 2 \\cdot (Area of square) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot 16 + 2 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&= 64 + 8 \\\\\n&= 72ft^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148727 #edb/ref 1065 2330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148727 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c41c924e-2d7e-5137-a601-92722cbb069a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148727 #edb/ref 1067 "Finding Surface Areas of Polyhedra Given Some Lengths" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354868 #edb/ref 1080 "274\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354868 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354868 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1636df6e-c36c-5694-809c-2595308f9d2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355597 #edb/ref 1080 "298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355597 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355597 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69be71f1-f11f-556a-b361-c708cd25bfdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356305 #edb/ref 1080 "302\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356305 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356305 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb726eac-67e6-52ae-b7ea-53cec9f6a137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356680 #edb/ref 1080 "286\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356680 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356680 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e65f7cbf-75d5-5323-9333-18983c300cd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356816 #edb/ref 1080 "264\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356816 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356816 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6da8cee-ac77-5205-b7d1-0164d6c5c262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186354868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186355597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357185 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "96f21fe4-6d0d-55f7-b1c7-8628d5f0c001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a6/a60731e7df54bb8f18f834b818c3e49c79fb30e67f7ed50c40f40aa813689ece.png)\n\nA manufacturer produces an unfair tetrahedral die from a plastic net, shown above. What is the total surface area of the die?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7e0efa5-6423-5a61-a04b-01649c479f66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357546 #edb/ref 1074 "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ base triangle and $3$ side triangles. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 64+3\\times 78 \\\\  & =64+234 \\\\  & =298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/24/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17e99f21-4a32-5f31-9b6f-4f7bf7f5a533" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392818 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](images/c3/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392819 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "56ae08df-7b65-5143-b632-e7f82228c84e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392820 #edb/ref 1080 "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392820 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392820 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7d05a27-bc22-599f-9521-686cccb47526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392821 #edb/ref 1080 "15\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392821 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392821 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b463f199-15d4-5666-95e5-3d376c7e7264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392822 #edb/ref 1080 "24\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921860